        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "8df94718bb0f8c325108e86fd106d0ebc97b24dd",
            "subject": "LU-20505 lfsck: fix osd-scrub vs lfsck race"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-28 22:36:45.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-28 23:59:42.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20505 osd-ldiskfs: advance scrub position after OI check",
        "message": "LU-20505 osd-ldiskfs: advance scrub position after OI check\n\nsanity-lfsck test_5 would fail with \"(13) Fail to generate linkEA\"\nor \"(5) unexpected status\" because the namespace LFSCK skipped\nobjects while the OI scrub was rebuilding the OI:\n\n  OIT scan failed at find target [0x200005221:0x1:0x0], cookie 198:\n  rc = -115\n  insert OI [0x200005221:0x1:0x0] -> 198/24953255\n\nosd_preload_next() stops a preload batch once it reaches\nos_pos_current, so the otable iterator caches the inode the scrub is\nworking on.  osd_scrub_next() advanced os_pos_current before that\ninode went through osd_scrub_check_update(), so the LFSCK lookup of\nthe object could find no OI mapping and get -EINPROGRESS, and LFSCK\nthen skipped the object and the entries of a skipped directory.\n\nAdvance os_pos_current in osd_scrub_exec() only after the inode has\nbeen checked and its OI mapping fixed.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-scrub\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lfsck env=ONLY=5,ONLY_MINUTES=30\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lfsck env=ONLY=5,ONLY_MINUTES=30\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lfsck env=ONLY=5,ONLY_MINUTES=30\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lfsck env=ONLY=5,ONLY_MINUTES=30\nFixes: e2ad44de38a4 (\"LU-9488 scrub: reset noslot for full speed scrub\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib684a0ee23d19b9ed079395fc95c02fefd3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
